===Etymology 2===
{{etymon|en|id=verb|:inh|enm:marchaundisen<ety:af<marchaundise<ety:bor<xno:marchaundise><fro:marcheandise>>><-en<id:infinitival>>>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|marchaundisen|t=to engage in commerce, traffic}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=marchaundīsen|pos=v|id=MED26874}}</ref> from {{m|enm|marchaundise|pos=noun}} (see [[#Etymology 1|etymology 1]]) + {{m|enm|-en|pos=suffix forming the {{glossary|infinitive}} of {{glossary|verb}}s}}.<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=-en|pos=''suf.''(3)|noformat=1|id=MED13518}}</ref>

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|en|merchandize||US}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmɜːt͡ʃəndaɪz/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmɝt͡ʃəndaɪz/|a=GA}}
* {{hyphenation|en|mer|chan|dise}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|archaic}} To engage in trade; to carry on [[commerce]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To engage in in-store promotion of the sale of goods, as by display and arrangement of goods.
#: {{ux|en|He started his career '''merchandising''' in a small clothing store chain.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|archaic}} To [[engage]] in the trade of.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To engage in in-store promotion of the sale of.
#: {{ux|en|He got hired to '''merchandise''' some new sporting goods lines.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To promote as if for sale.
#: {{ux|en|The record companies don't get as good a return on '''merchandising''' artists under contract.}}

